<h1 style="font-size:2rem;font-weight:800;">Integrations</h1>
<p>Connect UTMPro with your existing tools and workflows.</p>
<h2>Available Integrations</h2>
<table><tr><th>Integration</th><th>Category</th><th>Description</th></tr>
<tr><td>Stripe</td><td>Payment</td><td>Track revenue and manage billing</td></tr>
<tr><td>Shopify</td><td>Ecommerce</td><td>Track Shopify store sales</td></tr>
<tr><td>Zapier</td><td>Automation</td><td>Connect with 5000+ apps</td></tr>
<tr><td>Slack</td><td>Communication</td><td>Get click notifications</td></tr>
<tr><td>HubSpot</td><td>CRM</td><td>Sync leads to HubSpot</td></tr>
<tr><td>Google Analytics</td><td>Analytics</td><td>Send events to GA4</td></tr>
<tr><td>Segment</td><td>Analytics</td><td>Stream events to Segment</td></tr>
</table></div>
<h2>Connecting</h2>
<p>Go to <strong>Settings → Integrations</strong>, find the integration you want, click <strong>Connect</strong>, and provide the required configuration (usually an API key).</p>
<h2>Webhooks</h2>
<p>For custom integrations, use webhooks. Go to <strong>Settings → Webhooks</strong> to add a webhook URL that receives real-time events (link.clicked, lead.created, sale.completed).</p>
